{"id":"mahabharata-3-148","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":148,"title":"अष्टचत्वारिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 148 · Hanuman on the four ages","summary":{"en":"Bhima asks Hanuman to show the form in which he leapt the ocean. Hanuman first describes the four ages, Krita, Treta, Dvapara and Kali, and how dharma declines in each, and says that the age of his great form is past.","kn":"ಸಮುದ್ರ ಲಂಘಿಸಿದ ರೂಪವನ್ನು ತೋರಿಸೆಂದು ಭೀಮನು ಹನುಮಂತನನ್ನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹನುಮಂತನು ಮೊದಲು ಕೃತ, ತ್ರೇತಾ, ದ್ವಾಪರ, ಕಲಿ ಎಂಬ ನಾಲ್ಕು ಯುಗಗಳನ್ನೂ ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದರಲ್ಲಿ ಧರ್ಮ ಕ್ಷೀಣಿಸುವುದನ್ನೂ ವರ್ಣಿಸಿ, ತನ್ನ ಮಹಾರೂಪದ ಕಾಲ ಕಳೆದಿದೆ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीम हनुमान से समुद्र लाँघने वाला रूप दिखाने को कहते हैं। हनुमान पहले चार युगों, कृत, त्रेता, द्वापर और कलि, और प्रत्येक में धर्म के ह्रास का वर्णन करते हैं, और कहते हैं कि उनके महान रूप का युग बीत चुका है।","te":"సముద్రం లంఘించిన రూపాన్ని చూపమని భీముడు హనుమంతుని అడుగుతాడు. హనుమంతుడు మొదట కృత, త్రేతా, ద్వాపర, కలి అనే నాలుగు యుగాలను, ప్రతి దానిలో ధర్మం క్షీణించడాన్ని వర్ణించి, తన మహారూపపు కాలం గడిచిపోయిందంటాడు.","ta":"கடலைத் தாண்டிய உருவத்தைக் காட்டுமாறு பீமன் ஹனுமானைக் கேட்கிறான். ஹனுமான் முதலில் க்ருத, த்ரேதா, த்வாபர, கலி என்ற நான்கு யுகங்களையும் ஒவ்வொன்றிலும் அறம் தேய்வதையும் விவரித்து, தம் பேருருவின் காலம் கடந்துவிட்டது என்கிறார்.","ml":"സമുദ്രം ചാടിക്കടന്നപ്പോഴുള്ള രൂപം കാണിക്കാൻ ഭീമൻ ഹനുമാനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. ആദ്യം ഹനുമാൻ നാലു യുഗങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ച് പറയുന്നു: കൃതയുഗം, ത്രേതായുഗം, ദ്വാപരയുഗം, കലിയുഗം; ഓരോന്നിലും ധർമ്മം എങ്ങനെ ക്ഷയിക്കുന്നുവെന്നും, തന്റെ മഹാരൂപത്തിന്റെ യുഗം കഴിഞ്ഞുപോയെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.148; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तो महाबाहुर्भीमसेनः प्रतापवान् ।\nप्रणिपत्य ततः प्रीत्या भ्रातरं हृष्टमानसः ।\nउवाच श्लक्ष्णया वाचा हनूमन्तं कपीश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed thus, mighty and glorious Bhimasena bowed to his brother with affection, glad at heart, and spoke gently to Hanuman, lord of monkeys."}},{"n":2,"text":"मया धन्यतरो नास्ति यदार्यं दृष्टवानहम् ।\nअनुग्रहो मे सुमहांस्तृप्तिश्च तव दर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"No one is more fortunate than I, for I have seen my elder. This is a very great favour to me, and I am content at seeing you.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"एवं तु कृतमिच्छामि त्वयार्याद्य प्रियं मम ।\nयत्ते तदासीत्प्लवतः सागरं मकरालयम् ।\nरूपमप्रतिमं वीर तदिच्छामि निरीक्षितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Noble one, there is one more kindness I want you to do me: I wish to see that matchless form you had when you leapt the sea, the home of sea monsters.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"एवं तुष्टो भविष्यामि श्रद्धास्यामि च ते वचः ।\nएवमुक्तः स तेजस्वी प्रहस्य हरिरब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then I shall be satisfied and shall trust your words.\" Spoken to thus, the radiant monkey laughed and replied."}},{"n":5,"text":"न तच्छक्यं त्वया द्रष्टुं रूपं नान्येन केनचित् ।\nकालावस्था तदा ह्यन्या वर्तते सा न सांप्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You cannot see that form, nor can anyone else. That was a different state of time, and it is not the present one.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"अन्यः कृतयुगे कालस्त्रेतायां द्वापरेऽपरः ।\nअयं प्रध्वंसनः कालो नाद्य तद्रूपमस्ति मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The time of the Krita age was one thing, the Treta another, the Dvapara another. This is a time of decline, and I do not have that form today.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"भूमिर्नद्यो नगाः शैलाः सिद्धा देवा महर्षयः ।\nकालं समनुवर्तन्ते यथा भावा युगे युगे ।\nबलवर्ष्मप्रभावा हि प्रहीयन्त्युद्भवन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Earth, rivers, trees, mountains, Siddhas, gods and great sages all follow time, as conditions do from age to age. Strength, body and power wane and rise again.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"तदलं तव तद्रूपं द्रष्टुं कुरुकुलोद्वह ।\nयुगं समनुवर्तामि कालो हि दुरतिक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So enough of wanting to see that form, bearer of the Kuru line. I conform to the age, for time is hard to overcome.\""}},{"text":"भीम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"युगसंख्यां समाचक्ष्व आचारं च युगे युगे ।\nधर्मकामार्थभावांश्च वर्ष्म वीर्यं भवाभवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tell me the count of the ages and the conduct in each age, and the states of dharma, desire and wealth, the body, strength, and arising and passing.\""}},{"text":"हनूमानुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Hanuman said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"कृतं नाम युगं तात यत्र धर्मः सनातनः ।\nकृतमेव न कर्तव्यं तस्मिन्काले युगोत्तमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The age called Krita, dear one, is where dharma is eternal. In that best of ages nothing remained to be done, hence it was called Krita, 'done'.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"न तत्र धर्माः सीदन्ति न क्षीयन्ते च वै प्रजाः ।\nततः कृतयुगं नाम कालेन गुणतां गतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dharmas did not fail there, nor did people decline. Thus, through time, the Krita age came to have its name for its qualities.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"देवदानवगन्धर्वयक्षराक्षसपन्नगाः ।\nनासन्कृतयुगे तात तदा न क्रयविक्रयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the Krita age, dear one, there were no gods, danavas, gandharvas, yakshas, rakshasas or serpents as separate classes, and there was no buying and selling.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"न सामयजुऋग्वर्णाः क्रिया नासीच्च मानवी ।\nअभिध्याय फलं तत्र धर्मः संन्यास एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There were no distinctions of Sama, Yajus and Rig, no human effort. Fruit came by mere intention, and dharma was renunciation.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"न तस्मिन्युगसंसर्गे व्याधयो नेन्द्रियक्षयः ।\nनासूया नापि रुदितं न दर्पो नापि पैशुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In that age there were no diseases or decay of the senses, no spite, no weeping, no pride, no slander.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"न विग्रहः कुतस्तन्द्री न द्वेषो नापि वैकृतम् ।\nन भयं न च संतापो न चेर्ष्या न च मत्सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"No quarrel, so how could there be sloth? No hatred, no perversion, no fear, no anguish, no envy and no jealousy.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः परमकं ब्रह्म या गतिर्योगिनां परा ।\nआत्मा च सर्वभूतानां शुक्लो नारायणस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then the supreme Brahman, the highest goal of yogis, was there, and the white Narayana was the self of all beings.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"ब्राह्मणाः क्षत्रिया वैश्याः शूद्राश्च कृतलक्षणाः ।\nकृते युगे समभवन्स्वकर्मनिरताः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brahmins, Kshatriyas, Vaishyas and Shudras bore the marks of the Krita age, and in the Krita age the people were devoted to their own duties.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"समाश्रमं समाचारं समज्ञानमतीबलम् ।\nतदा हि समकर्माणो वर्णा धर्मानवाप्नुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Their stages of life, conduct, knowledge and great strength were equal; then the classes, equal in their actions, attained the dharmas.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"एकवेदसमायुक्ता एकमन्त्रविधिक्रियाः ।\nपृथग्धर्मास्त्वेकवेदा धर्ममेकमनुव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They were joined to a single Veda, with one set of mantras, rites and procedures. Though their dharmas differed, they had one Veda and followed one dharma.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"चातुराश्रम्ययुक्तेन कर्मणा कालयोगिना ।\nअकामफलसंयोगात्प्राप्नुवन्ति परां गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By action suited to the four stages of life, with time as its yoke, and by unattached fruit, they reached the highest goal.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"आत्मयोगसमायुक्तो धर्मोऽयं कृतलक्षणः ।\nकृते युगे चतुष्पादश्चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य शाश्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This dharma, joined to union with the self, bore the Krita marks. In the Krita age dharma is four-footed and eternal for the four classes.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"एतत्कृतयुगं नाम त्रैगुण्यपरिवर्जितम् ।\nत्रेतामपि निबोध त्वं यस्मिन्सत्रं प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is the age called Krita, free of the three qualities. Now learn of the Treta, in which sacrifice begins.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"पादेन ह्रसते धर्मो रक्ततां याति चाच्युतः ।\nसत्यप्रवृत्ताश्च नराः क्रियाधर्मपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In it dharma lessens by a quarter, and the unfallen Lord takes on redness. People are devoted to truth and to rites and dharma.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"ततो यज्ञाः प्रवर्तन्ते धर्माश्च विविधाः क्रियाः ।\nत्रेतायां भावसंकल्पाः क्रियादानफलोदयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then sacrifices begin, with dharmas and many kinds of rites. In the Treta, intentions arise from inclination, and rewards come from rites and gifts.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रचलन्ति न वै धर्मात्तपोदानपरायणाः ।\nस्वधर्मस्थाः क्रियावन्तो जनास्त्रेतायुगेऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"People of the Treta age, devoted to austerity and giving, did not stray from dharma; they stayed in their own duty and were active in rites.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"द्वापरेऽपि युगे धर्मो द्विभागोनः प्रवर्तते ।\nविष्णुर्वै पीततां याति चतुर्धा वेद एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"In the Dvapara age too, dharma goes on with two parts lost. Vishnu turns yellow, and the Veda itself is fourfold.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"ततोऽन्ये च चतुर्वेदास्त्रिवेदाश्च तथापरे ।\nद्विवेदाश्चैकवेदाश्चाप्यनृचश्च तथापरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then some know four Vedas, some three, others two or one, and others none of the Rik verses.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"एवं शास्त्रेषु भिन्नेषु बहुधा नीयते क्रिया ।\nतपोदानप्रवृत्ता च राजसी भवति प्रजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As the scriptures thus divide, rites are conducted in many ways, and people, intent on austerity and giving, become passionate.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"एकवेदस्य चाज्ञानाद्वेदास्ते बहवः कृताः ।\nसत्यस्य चेह विभ्रंशात्सत्ये कश्चिदवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Through ignorance of the one Veda, many Vedas were made; and through lapse from truth here, hardly anyone stays in truth.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"सत्यात्प्रच्यवमानानां व्याधयो बहवोऽभवन् ।\nकामाश्चोपद्रवाश्चैव तदा दैवतकारिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For those falling from truth, many diseases arose, along with desires and calamities, brought on by fate.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"यैरर्द्यमानाः सुभृशं तपस्तप्यन्ति मानवाः ।\nकामकामाः स्वर्गकामा यज्ञांस्तन्वन्ति चापरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tormented by these, people practise great austerity; some, full of desire, long for heaven and perform sacrifices.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"एवं द्वापरमासाद्य प्रजाः क्षीयन्त्यधर्मतः ।\nपादेनैकेन कौन्तेय धर्मः कलियुगे स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So, once Dvapara arrives, people decline through unrighteousness. In the Kali age, son of Kunti, dharma stands on one foot only.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"तामसं युगमासाद्य कृष्णो भवति केशवः ।\nवेदाचाराः प्रशाम्यन्ति धर्मयज्ञक्रियास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Reaching the dark age, Keshava becomes black. The Vedic conduct, dharma, sacrifices and rites die down.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"ईतयो व्याधयस्तन्द्री दोषाः क्रोधादयस्तथा ।\nउपद्रवाश्च वर्तन्ते आधयो व्याधयस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Calamities, diseases, sloth, faults like anger, and troubles, mental and bodily, appear.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"युगेष्वावर्तमानेषु धर्मो व्यावर्तते पुनः ।\nधर्मे व्यावर्तमाने तु लोको व्यावर्तते पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As the ages revolve, dharma turns away again; and when dharma turns away, the world turns away again.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"लोके क्षीणे क्षयं यान्ति भावा लोकप्रवर्तकाः ।\nयुगक्षयकृता धर्माः प्रार्थनानि विकुर्वते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When the world declines, the things that sustain it decline. Dharmas that bring about the age's end distort people's prayers.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"एतत्कलियुगं नाम अचिराद्यत्प्रवर्तते ।\nयुगानुवर्तनं त्वेतत्कुर्वन्ति चिरजीविनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is the age called Kali, which is soon to begin. Those long-lived follow the course of the ages.\""}},{"n":38,"text":"यच्च ते मत्परिज्ञाने कौतूहलमरिंदम ।\nअनर्थकेषु को भावः पुरुषस्य विजानतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"As for your curiosity to know me, scourge of enemies, what is the use to a knowing man of things that serve no purpose?\""}},{"n":39,"text":"एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ।\nयुगसंख्यां महाबाहो स्वस्ति प्राप्नुहि गम्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have told you all that you asked me, the count of the ages. May you be well, mighty-armed one; now go.\""}}]}]}